Task 1: Import assert.yml
Description Task 1: This task is designed to import a file named assert.yml. This file likely contains assert tasks that validate the system's state before performing any configuration.

Task 2: Install apache httpd
Description Task 2: This task is responsible for installing the Apache HTTP Server (httpd) on the target system. The package name is stored in the variable 'httpd_packages'.

Task 3: Configure selinux
Description Task 3: If SELinux is enabled on the system, this task will modify the SELinux settings using the variables 'httpd_sebooleans'. It will also allow connections to custom ports defined in 'httpd_port' and 'httpd_ssl_port'.

Task 4: Configure httpd
Description Task 4: This task is used to configure the Apache HTTP Server (httpd) using a template. The source of the template is stored in 'httpd_config_src' and the destination is stored in 'httpd_config_dest'. After the configuration, it will notify the handlers to test the configuration validity and restart the httpd service.

Task 5: Activate httpd module | Debian
Description Task 5: If the target system is running a Debian-based OS, this task is used to activate specific httpd modules. The names of the modules are stored in 'httpd_modules_to_activate_with_command'. After activation, it will notify the handlers to test the configuration validity.

Task 6: Import ssl.yml
Description Task 6: If SSL is enabled, this task is designed to import a file named ssl.yml. This file likely contains tasks related to configuring SSL for httpd.

Task 7: Import locations.yml
Description Task 7: If 'httpd_locations' is defined, this task will import a file named locations.yml. This file likely contains tasks related to configuring locations for httpd.

Task 8: Import vhosts.yml
Description Task 8: If 'httpd_vhosts' is defined, this task will import a file named vhosts.yml. This file likely contains tasks related to configuring virtual hosts for httpd.

Task 9: Configure ports
Description Task 9: If the target system is running a Debian-based or SUSE-based OS, this task is used to configure ports for httpd using a template. The source of the template is stored in 'httpd_ports_conf' and the destination is stored in 'httpd_server_root/httpd_ports_conf'. After the configuration, it will notify the handlers to test the configuration validity and restart the httpd service.

Task 10: Import directories.yml
Description Task 10: If 'httpd_directories' is defined, this task will import a file named directories.yml. This file likely contains tasks related to creating and configuring directories for httpd.

Task 11: Flush handlers
