content=' ```yaml\n---\n- name: Install epel\n  yum:\n    name: epel-release\n  when: >\n    ansible_os_family == \'RedHat\' and (\n    (ansible_distribution == \'Amazon\' and ansible_distribution_major_version == \'2\') or\n    (ansible_distribution in [\'RedHat\', \'CentOS\'] and ansible_distribution_major_version in [\'7\', \'8\', \'9\', \'10\']))\n\n- name: Install epel gpg key\n  rpm_key:\n    state: present\n    key: "{{ epel_gpg_key }}"\n\n- name: Install epel-release\n  yum:\n    name: "{{ epel_url }}"\n  notify: Update package cache\n\n- name: Install epel-next-release\n  yum:\n    name: "{{ epel_next_url }}"\n  notify: Update package cache\n  when: epel_next | bool\n```\n\nIn this Ansible playbook:\n\n- Task 1 and 2 are executed for all systems that match the specified conditions.\n- Task 3 is always executed after Task 1 and 2.\n- Task 4 is executed only when the variable "epel_next" is true.\n- The "notify" directive ensures that the handler "Update package cache" is triggered after Task 3 and 4 are completed.\n- The "rpm_key" module is used to manage RPM keys, and the "yum" module is used to install packages.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'codestral:22b', 'created_at': '2025-10-16T07:36:33.45347301Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 9067917243, 'load_duration': 17120367, 'prompt_eval_count': 536, 'prompt_eval_duration': 534341416, 'eval_count': 365, 'eval_duration': 8514172171, 'model_name': 'codestral:22b'} id='run--42ee677f-8df9-468a-9412-a4b720ed9d52-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 536, 'output_tokens': 365, 'total_tokens': 901}
